Description: DTK tray applet for distribution-agnostic package update management
 Monitors and manages system package updates, installations, removals,
 purges and residual cleanup, with dependency resolution and security advisories.
 .
 Supports multiple package backends via pluggable modules: apt/dpkg on
 Debian/Ubuntu/UOS/Deepin, dnf/rpm on Fedora/openEuler, and the linyaps
 (linglong) sandboxed app ecosystem, with per-distribution auto-detection.
 .
 Provides two tray integrations: a native dde-dock plugin (for Deepin/UOS
 desktop) and a generic Qt system tray (freedesktop, no dde-dock dependency),
 plus a standalone GUI and an optional D-Bus/systemd user daemon.
 .
 The active package manager is auto-detected per distribution; install the
 corresponding backend package (apt/dpkg, dnf/rpm, or linyaps) to enable
 updates on your system.
